[
  "The research domain of mesoscale cell biology specifically focuses on biomolecular condensates formed through liquid-liquid phase separation. A significant scientific gap remains because current siloed datasets do not provide a unified, quantitative framework linking molecular sequence features to network-level interactions and cellular-scale phenotypes to explain context-dependent condensation. The primary objective is to predict and mechanistically explain the cellular-scale properties of these condensates by training graph neural networks and multi-modal representation models. To achieve this, public datasets covering molecular sequences, protein interaction networks, and in vivo biochemical states will be harmonized into multi-scale feature vectors using a unified ontology and cross-reference mapping pipeline anchored on UniProt accessions. This research will contribute a quantitative, multi-scale model of context-dependent condensate formation and establish a generalizable framework for studying mesoscale emergence across biological scales."
