abstract_text:
[
  "The research domain of mesoscale biology focuses on the emergent properties and liquid-liquid phase separation of biomolecular condensates. A critical scientific gap is the lack of understanding of the molecular grammar that dictates how atomic-level interactions scale up to govern mesoscale condensation, largely due to isolated data silos that disconnect spatial and temporal dimensions. The primary objective is to build Mesoscale-CondensateNet, an artificial intelligence-driven predictive model that maps molecular features to emergent mesoscale properties and cellular outcomes using multi-modal graph neural networks and large language models. Public datasets spanning structural, interaction, and phase-separating protein databases will be integrated into a highly annotated Mesoscale Knowledge Graph where molecules are embedded as nodes and condition-specific interactions serve as weighted edges. This research is significant because it shifts the field from descriptive studies to predictive models of cellular organization, aiding future developments in neurodegenerative diseases and synthetic biology."
]

